Corosync on NetBSD
==================

Two settings differ from what the upstream documentation assumes.

Socket buffers.  libknet asks for 8 MB socket buffers and, when corosync
runs as root, refuses to create the link if the kernel will not give
them.  NetBSD's default kern.sbmax (262144) will not, and corosync then
exits at start-up with

	knet_handle_new failed: File name too long (63)

Set, in /etc/sysctl.conf,

	kern.sbmax=16777216

The rc.d script checks this and will not start corosync below it.

Crypto model.  corosync uses the nss crypto model unless told otherwise,
and this build of kronosnet has only the openssl one.  With encryption
enabled, name it in the totem section of corosync.conf:

	totem {
		crypto_model: openssl
		crypto_cipher: aes256
		crypto_hash: sha256
		...
	}

Without it corosync exits with "this version of libknet was built
without nss support".

The example configuration is in @PREFIX@/share/examples/corosync.
Generate the shared key with corosync-keygen.
